<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 21,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 21,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd on Wednesday jointly bought 21,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp, company officials said.  </p>
<p>Of the total, Cheiljedang bought 11,000 tonnes at basis prices over July futures on the U.S grain futures exchanges including the Chicago Board of Trade, they said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour purchased the remaining 10,000 tonnes at fixed prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for June 5-July 5 to the western port of Inchon.  </p>
